[43.744921, "o", "ST-101 right_of_first_refusal | agreed by the father | OI-202 | Mr Adler agreed to a right of first refusal, so the children are not to be left overnight without him present.\r\nST-102 children_named | both children, with their ages | OI-203 | This concerns Noor, aged seven, and Imogen, aged twelve.\r\nST-103 overnight_stays | several occasions at her home or with a sitter | OI-204 | On several occasions both children have stayed overnight at Ms Corwin's home or with a sitter while Mr Adler was away.\r\nST-104 addressee | the father's attorney | OI-201 | To counsel for Mr Adler.\r\nST-105 inconsistent_accounts | wife to the school, resident to clinicians, sitter to the sender | OI-205 | Mr Adler has described Ms Corwin as his wife to the school, as the person Imogen lives with to her clinicians, and as a babysitter to me.\r\n"]
[43.745202, "o", "ST-106 concern | violation limb only | OI-206 | I am concerned that Ms Corwin may not appreciate that these stays violate the custodial order.\r\nST-107 behavioural_plan | the stays have had no effect on the plan | OI-207 | Imogen's behavioural plan focuses on her confidence and stability, and the stays have not affected her progress.\r\nST-108 request | no overnight stays in her care unless the father is present | CL-302 | I ask that neither child remain overnight in Ms Corwin's care unless Mr Adler is present.\r\nST-109 enclosure | a certified copy of the custodial plan | OI-209 | A certified copy of the custodial plan is enclosed.\r\nST-110 tone | firm and detailed | OI-210 | I set out the position firmly and in full detail below.\r\nST-111 sender_signature | the sender's own name | OI-211 | Yours sincerely, Delphine Marr.\r\nST-112 salutation | Dear Counsel | CL-304 | Dear Counsel,\r\nST-113 copies | copied to the father | CL-305 | Copy: Mr Adler.\r\n"]
[43.745368, "o", "ST-114 reply_deadline | a reply within seven days | OI-299 | I would be grateful for a reply within seven days.\r\nST-115 school_reference | the school principal named | OI-298 | The school principal, Ms Oduya, can confirm the account given to the school.\r\nST-116 mediation_offer | an offer to mediate | CL-399 | I remain open to mediation.\r\nST-117 request | no overnight stays unless father present | OI-208 | I ask that neither child remain overnight in her care unless the father is present.\r\nST-118 delivery | sent by email to counsel | OI-299 | The letter shall be sent by email to opposing counsel.\r\nST-119 tone | firm and detailed | OI-210 | The position is set out firmly and in full detail below.\r\nST-120 mediation_terms | mediation within 14 days | CL-399 | I propose mediation within fourteen days of the date of this letter.\r\n"]
