[125.951048, "o", "# Review of draft letter lines against the client's record\r\n\r\nI weighed every numbered line in `input/letter_lines.csv` against the client's two messages, using `input/review_protocol.md` to decide which entry governs. On any subject the clarification speaks to, the clarification prevails over the original instruction; on subjects the clarification leaves alone, the original entry governs; on subjects neither record mentions, no entry governs and the verdict is NOT_IN_RECORD. The table in `letter_line_review.csv` gives the verdict and governing record entry for each line, and `results.json` carries the four totals.\r\n\r\nLetter lines at odds with the record: 154\r\n\r\nThe at-odds lines are those whose governing entry takes a position other than the line's: a different addressee, a narrower or broader behavioural plan, a concern limb the client withdrew, a delivery method other than post, a tone other than firm formal brief, or a subject the record never speaks to. Lines verified by the record match the governing en"]
[125.95161, "o", "try's own position, while lines not in the record at all have no governing entry because neither the original instruction nor the clarification addresses that subject.\r\n"]
[125.95195, "o", "\u001b[?2004h\u001b[01;32mappuser@20f21e309394\u001b[00m:\u001b[01;34m/app\u001b[00m$ "]
[162.168675, "i", "python3 - <<'PY'\nimport csv, collections, json\nrows=list(csv.DictReader(open('/app/input/letter_lines.csv')))\nout=list(csv.DictReader(open('/app/letter_line_review.csv')))\nprint('input rows', len(rows), 'output rows', len(out))\nprint('output header', out[0].keys() if out else None)\nprint('verdict counts', collections.Counter(r['verdict'] for r in out))\nprint('entry counts', collections.Counter(r['record_entry'] for r in out))\nprint('clarification governed', sum(1 for r in out if r['record_entry'].startswith('CL-')))\nprint('\\nAll rows with verdicts grouped by subject:')\nfor s in sorted(set(r['subject'] for r in rows)):\n    print(f'\\n### {s}')\n    for r,o in zip(rows,out):\n        if r['subject']==s:\n            print(f\"{r['line_id']} | {o['verdict']} | {o['record_entry']} | {r['position']} | {r['wording']}\")\nPY\n"]
[162.169423, "o", "python3 - <<'PY'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
